"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-11-10","finding":"Policies Comply with Rules: It was observed that the operational policies did not include statements in regard to the contact information for Child Care Regulation under Health and Human Services as the information listed was for the Department of Family and Protective Services. In addition, there were no statements regarding Infant safe sleep, hearing and vision screening, water activities, promotion of indoor and outdoor activities, insect repellent, sunscreen, epinephrine/medications and  inclusive care in regard to special needs children in accordance to the updated minimum standards requirements.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026434320","violation_type_title":"Policies Comply with Rules (26 TAC §746.201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1162678-i20231107-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407-12","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1162678-i20231107","date":"2023-11-07","original_code":"746.3407(12)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Mark Cleaning Supplies, Toxic Materials; Keep Separate from Food and Inaccessible to Children: A clear bottle of hand sanitizer located on the sink of the main hallway near the older three -year-old classroom was accessible to children. This was corrected when the director placed the hand sanitizer in a locked closet out of reach of children.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026273634","violation_type_title":"Mark Cleaning Supplies, Toxic Materials; Keep Separate from Food and Inaccessible to Children (26 TAC §746.3407(12))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1162678-i20231107-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2421-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1162678-i20231107","date":"2023-11-07","original_code":"746.2421(b)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-11-09","finding":"Written Feeding Instructions - Review and Update Every 30 Days: There were a total of 9 infant children present at the time of inspection without current feeding instructions on file that had been signed by a parent/guardian within 30 days. Three of the feeding instructions were corrected during inspection when the parents updated the forms.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026474214","violation_type_title":"Written Feeding Instructions - Review and Update Every 30 Days (26 TAC §746.2421(b))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1162678-i20231107-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1162678-i20231107","date":"2023-11-07","original_code":"746.3407","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2023-12-27","finding":"Maintenance of Building, Grounds and Equipment: The fence and picket along the school age playground  was leaning creating entrapment and entanglement risk to children that utilize the playground.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026313896","violation_type_title":"Maintenance of Building, Grounds and Equipment (26 TAC §746.3407)","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1162678-i20221108","date":"2022-11-08","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905805558","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905805558","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-11-08","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1162678-i20220419","date":"2022-04-19","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_re